# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Line endings
#
# Windows ends lines with CRLF, Linux and macOS with LF. Without a rule,
# Git warns on every file and members on different systems can end up
# with diffs showing every line changed when nothing actually did.
#
# "text=auto eol=lf" means: store everything as LF in the repository,
# and let each machine check it out however it likes. This is the
# standard arrangement and silences the CRLF warning.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be converted — doing so corrupts them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip  binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary

# Batch files genuinely need CRLF to run correctly on Windows.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
